quizData.question:
How does short-circuit evaluation affect the execution of this code?

```java
int a = 10, b = 5;
if (a > 20 && ++b > 5) {
    System.out.print("True ");
}
System.out.println(b);
```

What will be the final printed value of `num` after this loop executes?

```java
int num = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    if (i == 3) break;
    num += i;
}
System.out.println(num);
```

What is the output of the following nested loop?

```java
int count = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
    for (int j = 1; j <= 2; j++) {
        count++;
    }
}
System.out.println(count);
```

What is the output of the following `while` loop snippet?

```java
int k = 1;
while (k < 10) {
    k *= 2;
}
System.out.println(k);
```

What is the output of the following `switch` code due to fall-through?

```java
int day = 2;
switch (day) {
    case 1: System.out.print("Mon ");
    case 2: System.out.print("Tue ");
    case 3: System.out.print("Wed ");
        break;
    default: System.out.print("Sun ");
}
```

What will be printed when running this `do-while` loop?

```java
int count = 5;
do {
    System.out.print(count + " ");
    count++;
} while (count < 5);
```
